{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun surprisingly sharp against his eyelids. He sat up in bed, a strange awareness washing over him – an awareness of textures, of code subtly shimmering beneath the mundane reality of his bedroom. The floral wallpaper seemed overly detailed, the sunlight rendered with an unnatural brilliance. He reached for his glasses, and as his fingers brushed the bedside table, a notification popped up in his vision: \"Inventory: Bedside Table (Standard Issue)\". Panic tightened his chest. He looked at his hands, noticing the perfectly symmetrical lines of his skin, the unnervingly smooth texture. A quest log materialized in his peripheral vision: \"Objective: Consume Breakfast. Reward: +5 Health.\" This wasn't his life. This was… a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, navigating the familiar layout of his house with newfound caution. Every object felt pre-programmed, every interaction governed by unseen rules. His reflection in the hallway mirror showed a character model – slightly generic, undeniably him, but lacking the subtle imperfections of a real person. He cautiously opened the refrigerator, a shimmering UI overlay appearing with options like \"Milk (2 units),\" \"Eggs (6 units),\" and \"Bacon (4 units).\" Arthur stared, utterly bewildered. He picked up a carton of milk, the weight feeling oddly… simulated. He had to figure out how this happened, how to escape this digital prison. But for now, he had a quest to complete, and the promise of +5 Health.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4622840881347656}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0001805857609724626}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.07861142605543137}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -0.916972279548645}, {"token": "▁sun", "logprob": -0.12192082405090332}, {"token": "▁surprisingly", "logprob": -1.3393